{"summary":"DCT MCP Server: assistant does not treat \"compliance node\" as a Continuous Compliance engine","description":{"type":"doc","version":1,"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"project repo - https://github.com/delphix/dxi-mcp-server , main branch"}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Problem"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Feedback from a colleague while testing the DCT AI Assistant / DCT MCP Server (2026.1.0.0): the assistant does not know that a "},{"type":"text","text":"compliance node","marks":[{"type":"strong"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is the same thing as a "},{"type":"text","text":"masking engine","marks":[{"type":"strong"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (canonical term: "},{"type":"text","text":"Continuous Compliance engine","marks":[{"type":"strong"}]},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The colleague expected the assistant to explain that there are "},{"type":"text","text":"two different approaches to use a compliance engine","marks":[{"type":"strong"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Findings (code review of "},{"type":"text","text":"dxi-mcp-server","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":")"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"src/dct_mcp_server/config/server_instructions.md","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" terminology table (Continuous Compliance engine row) lists the accepted aliases as \"CC engine, Compliance Engine, engine, appliance\". "},{"type":"text","text":"\"Compliance node\" is not listed","marks":[{"type":"strong"}]},{"type":"text","text":", so the model has no instruction to map it."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"src/dct_mcp_server/config/mappings/vocabulary.txt","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" maps "},{"type":"text","text":"masking engine","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" to "},{"type":"text","text":"Continuous Compliance engine","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":". That map only rewrites upstream text (error bodies, OpenAPI summaries); it does not affect user input."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Nothing in the repo describes two approaches for using a compliance engine, so the assistant has no basis to give that explanation."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Expected behaviour"}]},{"type":"orderedList","attrs":{"order":1},"content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"Compliance node\", \"compliance engine\" and \"masking engine\" in user input are all understood as a Continuous Compliance engine, and the answer uses the canonical term."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"When a user asks how to use a compliance engine, the assistant explains the two approaches. "},{"type":"text","text":"The two approaches still need to be defined by the feature owner (open question).","marks":[{"type":"strong"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Proposed fix"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Add \"compliance node\" as an accepted alias in the "},{"type":"text","text":"server_instructions.md","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" terminology table and the \"Rules (read first)\" block. That block must stay within the first 4,000 characters."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirm the term against the PPM-1129 glossary (v1.2). If it is not in the glossary, add it there."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Add the two-approaches guidance once defined."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Add a regression test in "},{"type":"text","text":"tests/unit/test_vocabulary_regression.py","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" and a row in the 2026.1.0.0 test-case workbook (Live DCT Agent Checks)."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Acceptance criteria"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Prompt \"Which compliance node is registered in DCT?\" (and the same with \"masking engine\") returns Continuous Compliance engines and does not say \"node\" or \"Masking Engine\" back to the user."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Asking how to use a compliance engine produces the agreed two-approach explanation."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Regression test fails if the alias is removed."}]}]}]}]},"issuetype":{"self":"https://perforce.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issuetype/10016","id":"10016","description":"A problem or error.","iconUrl":"https://perforce.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/12900?size=medium","name":"Bug","subtask":false,"avatarId":12900,"hierarchyLevel":0},"parent":{"id":"1718174","key":"APIGW-28246","self":"https://perforce.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/1718174","fields":{"summary":"DCT AI Assistant: Deliver General Availability (GA)","status":{"self":"https://perforce.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/status/3","description":"This work item is being actively worked on at the moment by the assignee.","iconUrl":"https://perforce.atlassian.net/images/icons/statuses/inprogress.png","name":"In Progress","id":"3","statusCategory":{"self":"https://perforce.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/statuscategory/4","id":4,"key":"indeterminate","colorName":"yellow","name":"In Progress"}},"priority":{"self":"https://perforce.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/priority/12096","iconUrl":"https://perforce.atlassian.net/images/icons/priorities/major.svg","name":"P2","id":"12096"},"issuetype":{"self":"https://perforce.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issuetype/10000","id":"10000","description":"A collection of related bugs, stories, and tasks.","iconUrl":"https://perforce.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10307?size=medium","name":"Epic","subtask":false,"avatarId":10307,"hierarchyLevel":1}}},"labels":["AI-IN-PROGRESS","PPM-1129","dct-mcp-server","vocabulary"],"components":[{"self":"https://perforce.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/component/25036","id":"25036","name":"Core - AI Platform"}],"reporter":{"self":"https://perforce.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=632990d9234d44d406ced9e5","accountId":"632990d9234d44d406ced9e5","emailAddress":"vinay.byrappa@perforce.com","avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7a06e1c2fe2cf73086ff746f6103e5de?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FVB-4.png","24x24":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7a06e1c2fe2cf73086ff746f6103e5de?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FVB-4.png","16x16":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7a06e1c2fe2cf73086ff746f6103e5de?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FVB-4.png","32x32":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7a06e1c2fe2cf73086ff746f6103e5de?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FVB-4.png"},"displayName":"Vinay Byrappa","active":true,"timeZone":"America/Chicago","accountType":"atlassian"},"assignee":{"self":"https://perforce.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=632990d9234d44d406ced9e5","accountId":"632990d9234d44d406ced9e5","emailAddress":"vinay.byrappa@perforc